defklown wrote:
> Magic traps suck, especially rust traps and polymorph traps.

Magic traps are specific traps that (in most cases) create a horde of
monsters, and they are to be distinguished from, eg., polymorph traps;
so I'd avoid the _generic_ term "magic trap" in Nethack.

> Aside from
> having the searching intrinsic (ring of searching, excalibur, level 9
> monk, level 10 archeologist/rogue/tourist, or level 1 ranger) how does
> one avoid magic traps?

It's always possible to use the 's' command, but heavy use of searching
will make you hungry quickly; so it's a trade-off.

> I know that certain traps can only appear below
> certain levels, but other than that, are there any ways to
> avoid/foresee magic traps? And levitation doesn't protect you from
> magic traps, right?

You can foresee polymorph traps by monsters of unusual high level to
be seen around. You cannot foresee magic traps, but occasionally you
may detect some monster with burnt armor that may be the effect either
of a fire trap or of a magic trap (which sometimes emits fire).

You mentioned the dungeon level, and that's a really good point to
keep in mind! Personally I am very cautious when I'm on a level where
any precious armor can be destroyed by polytraps.

> I'm aware that wearing an amulet of unchanging and a ring of polymorph
> control can protect you from the effects of a polymorph trap, and
> rustproofing your armor and weapon can protect you from the effects of
> a rust trap, but there are some magic traps whose effects you can't
> protect yourself from, and I'd like to know how to avoid/foresee magic
> traps, specifically. 

The inherent property of a trap is that you usually don't see it; the
bad guy who set-up a trap *don't want* you to find it.

(Your question reminds me on a scene in the "The Gamers" video. :-)

> Tips regarding non-magic traps are welcome too.

Rocks, arrows, and bolts on the floor can be a sign of a trap. Rusted,
burnt armor from killed monsters is typically a sign of traps on that
level. Some boulder in a room (or cave) may be a sign for a rolling
boulder trap. I already mentioned exceptional monsters and polytraps.
On levels with spiders there may be spider webs. When in some corridor
monsters avoid stepping on a certain empty square that's a heavy sign
of a trap. There are also specific sounds associated with some traps,
bear traps and rolling boulder traps, that you may hear from distance.

